# Top-level runtime dependencies: the only file to edit by hand.
#
# requirements.txt is compiled from this file into a fully resolved,
# hash-pinned lock (every transitive package, every artifact hash), so a build
# installs exactly what CI audited and nothing a compromised or re-published
# upstream release could swap in. CI's backend-audit job recompiles it on every
# push, keeping the committed pins, and uploads it as the `backend-lock-<sha>`
# artifact. After changing a pin here, commit that file as
# backend/requirements.txt; never hand-edit the lock. Dependabot regenerates
# both files together. tests/test_dependency_pins.py fails if the two disagree
# on a pin or the lock loses its hashes.
fastapi==0.141.1
